{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    fib4_values = [0, 0, 2, 0] # Represents fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib4 = fib4_values[3] + fib4_values[2] + fib4_values[1] + fib4_values[0]\n        fib4_values[0] = fib4_values[1]\n        fib4_values[1] = fib4_values[2]\n        fib4_values[2] = fib4_values[3]\n        fib4_values[3] = next_fib4\n\n    return fib4_values[3]"}
